kettle|water-boiling-vessel|NOUN|vessel for boiling water|A container with a handle and a spout, used to heat water until it boils.|ấm đun nước|The electric kettle switched off while An arranged cups on the tray.|Ấm đun nước điện tự tắt khi An đang xếp cốc lên khay.|Countable; boil water in a kettle. A kettle heats water; a teapot is primarily for brewing or serving tea.|-
proceed|continue-an-activity|VERB|continue an activity|To continue doing something or move on to the next stage.|tiếp tục; tiến hành|Once everyone had read the plan, the team proceeded with the repairs.|Khi mọi người đã đọc kế hoạch, cả nhóm tiếp tục công việc sửa chữa.|Intransitive: proceed with something, proceed to do something. Formal compared with continue.|0
proceed|move-onward|VERB|move towards a place|To move onwards in a particular direction.|đi tiếp|Passengers were asked to proceed to the waiting area beside the gate.|Hành khách được yêu cầu đi tiếp đến khu vực chờ bên cạnh cổng.|Intransitive; proceed to a place or along a route. Common in formal directions.|1
thirty|number-30|NUMBER|number 30|The number that is ten more than twenty.|ba mươi|Thirty seedlings fitted into the wooden tray.|Ba mươi cây con vừa trong chiếc khay gỗ.|Cardinal number; thirty seedlings. Thirtieth is the ordinal; thirties can name a decade or age range.|0
weather|atmospheric-conditions|NOUN|conditions outdoors|The conditions of the air outdoors, such as rain, temperature and wind.|thời tiết|The weather stayed dry while we repaired the roof.|Thời tiết vẫn khô ráo trong lúc chúng tôi sửa mái nhà.|Uncountable: fine weather, a spell of wet weather. Climate describes longer-term patterns.|0
deserve|merit-a-result|VERB|be worthy of something|To be worthy of receiving something because of what you have done or what you are like.|xứng đáng được|The volunteers deserve recognition for keeping the shelter open.|Những tình nguyện viên xứng đáng được ghi nhận vì đã duy trì hoạt động của nơi trú tạm.|Transitive: deserve something or to do something. Deserve can concern praise or punishment.|0
